<article class="m2-page" id="p-controls-mappings" data-group="Buttons &amp; Scripts" data-title="Remap buttons and keys" data-time="4 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Buttons &amp; Scripts</p>
    <h1>Remap buttons and keys</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Any button, key or mouse click will send whatever you choose.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Mouse &amp; keyboard</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Controller</span><span class="m2-time">4 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-controls-mappings--open-mappings">
    <h2>1. Open Mappings</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>On HOME, tap <b>Settings</b> on the game picture.</li>
      <li>Tap <b>Mappings</b> ("Rebind any button to any button").</li>
      <li>Tap <b>Switch ›</b> to pick what you're remapping: <b>Controller</b> or <b>Mouse &amp; Keyboard</b>.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'exo2-ann-remap.webp' | asset_url }}" width="786" height="1704" loading="lazy" alt="Mappings for the controller. A: Showing Controller, Switch. B: the Bindings list heading. C: the Cross row, a binding you can tap. Other rows show default.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-MAP.1 — Mappings, controller view</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>Letter</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">A</span></td><td><b>Showing Controller</b> · <b>Switch ›</b></td><td>Swap to the mouse and keyboard view.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">B</span></td><td><b>Bindings</b></td><td>"What each button, key and click sends."</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">C</span></td><td>A binding row (<b>Cross</b>)</td><td>Tap to change what it sends. <b>default</b> means unchanged.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-controls-mappings--change-a-button">
    <h2>2. Change what a button sends</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Tap the row of the button you want to change, for example <b>Circle</b>.</li>
      <li>Under <b>Choose what it should send.</b>, pick a tab: <b>Pad</b>, <b>Mouse</b>, <b>A–T</b>, <b>U–0</b>, <b>Esc…</b> or <b>F-keys</b>.</li>
      <li>Tap the button or key it should send. The <b>SENDS</b> box updates.</li>
      <li>Optional: tap <b>Behaves</b> to change how it acts (see the table below).</li>
      <li>Tap <b>✕</b> to close. It saves by itself.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-mp-press.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Which button do you want to change. 1: press the button you want on your keyboard, mouse or controller. 2: or tap it in the list, here R2.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-MAP.2 — Which button do you want to change?</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Press it</b></td><td>That press isn't sent to the game.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Or tap it</b></td><td>Controller, Keyboard and Mouse tabs.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-mp-sends.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="The Circle button's panel. 1: Sends, Circle. 2: Behaves, While I hold it. 3: Cross, the new output. 4: Unbind, send nothing.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-MAP.3 — A button's panel</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Sends</b></td><td>What this button does in the game now.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Behaves</b></td><td>While you hold it, toggle, and more.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>New output</b></td><td>Tap it, then tap Save at the top.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">4</span></td><td><b>Unbind (send nothing)</b></td><td>The button sends nothing at all.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'exo2-ann-remap-2.webp' | asset_url }}" width="786" height="1704" loading="lazy" alt="Remapping Circle. A: Behaves, While I hold it. B: Sends Circle. C: the Pad tab of the picker, with Mouse, A to T, U to 0, Esc and F-keys tabs. D: Unbind, send nothing.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-MAP.4 — Mappings, Circle open</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>Letter</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">A</span></td><td><b>Behaves</b></td><td>How the button acts when you press it.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">B</span></td><td><b>SENDS</b></td><td>What this button sends now.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">C</span></td><td><b>Pad</b> tab</td><td>Pick a controller button. Other tabs hold mouse buttons and keys.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">D</span></td><td><b>Unbind (send nothing)</b></td><td>The button does nothing in the game.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Behaves</th><th>What happens</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Behaves"><b>While I hold it</b> (default)</td><td data-label="What happens">Sends while you hold the button, like normal.</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Behaves"><b>On, then off</b></td><td data-label="What happens">Press once to turn it on, press again to turn it off (a toggle).</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Behaves"><b>Only a quick tap</b></td><td data-label="What happens">Sends only on a quick tap. Set the time under <b>A quick tap is under</b> (1–60000 ms, step 25, default 200 ms).</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Behaves"><b>Only a long hold</b></td><td data-label="What happens">Sends only after you hold it. Set <b>Hold it for</b> (1–60000 ms, step 25, default 200 ms).</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-controls-mappings--keyboard-and-mouse">
    <h2>Keyboard and mouse view</h2>
    <p>In the <b>Mouse &amp; Keyboard</b> view, tap any key on the drawn keyboard, or a mouse button (<b>M1</b>–<b>M5</b>, <b>Wheel</b>). Colours show which keys are held, mapped, or run a Script.</p>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'exo2-ann-keyboard-map.webp' | asset_url }}" width="786" height="1704" loading="lazy" alt="The keyboard and mouse map. A: Showing Mouse and Keyboard, Switch. B: a full keyboard plus mouse buttons M1 to M5 and the wheel. C: Bigger keys. D: the Bindings list, with W to Left Stick Up, S to Left Stick Down and more.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-MAP.5 — Mappings, mouse and keyboard view</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>Letter</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">A</span></td><td><b>Showing Mouse &amp; Keyboard</b></td><td>Swap back to the controller view.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">B</span></td><td>The keyboard</td><td>Tap a key to map it.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">C</span></td><td><b>Bigger keys</b></td><td>Zooms the keyboard for easier tapping.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">D</span></td><td><b>Bindings</b></td><td>Every key and click, and what it sends.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--tip"><p class="m2-call-label">Tip</p><p>Want one button to do two jobs? Use a shift layer: <b>Add a shift layer</b>, choose the button you hold, then the button you press, then what it sends.</p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-controls-mappings--scripts">
    <h2>Buttons used by Scripts</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>In <b>Bindings</b>, a row that reads <b>Replaced by Script</b> (1) starts a Script. Tap <b>View script</b> to open it.</li>
      <li>A row that reads <b>Not bound</b> (2) sends nothing.</li>
      <li>Open <b>Scripts</b> at the bottom of Mappings to switch each Script on or off.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-mp-scripts.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Mappings, Bindings. 1: Cross, Replaced by Script: Jump shot, with View script. 2: Circle, Not bound.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-MAP.6 — Settings › Mappings › Bindings</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Replaced by Script</b></td><td>This button starts a Script.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Not bound</b></td><td>This button sends nothing.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-mp-list.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Mappings, the Scripts list for this config. 1: Scripts, 3 on this config. 2: a Script's on and off switch. 3: Add a button.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-MAP.7 — Settings › Mappings › Scripts</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Scripts</b></td><td>Shows or hides the Scripts on this config.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Switch</b></td><td>Turns one Script on or off.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>Add a button</b></td><td>Gives another button its own mapping or Script.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-controls-mappings--check-it-worked">
    <h2>Check it worked</h2>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--check"><p class="m2-call-label">Check it worked</p>
      <p>You're set when all of these are true:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>App:</b> the row shows your new choice instead of <b>default</b>.</li>
        <li><b>Game:</b> pressing the button does the new action.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Not seeing one? <a href="#p-help-scripts">A script or button won't fire</a></p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-controls-mappings--next">
    <h2>Next</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Recommended:</b> <a href="#p-scripts-explained">Scripts explained</a></li>
      <li><a href="#p-scripts-library">Ready-made Scripts</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</article>


<article class="m2-page" id="p-scripts-explained" data-group="Buttons &amp; Scripts" data-title="Scripts explained" data-time="3 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Buttons &amp; Scripts</p>
    <h1>Scripts explained</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">What a Script is, where Scripts live, and when they run.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Mouse &amp; keyboard</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Controller</span><span class="m2-time">3 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-explained--how-it-works">
    <h2>How a Script works</h2>
    <p>A Script is a button that presses other buttons for you. It has two parts:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>When</b>: what starts it. For example, "When I press R2" or "Over and over while I hold it".</li>
      <li><b>Do this</b>: the steps it presses, in order. Taps, holds, waits and stick pushes.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Scripts run on the EXO itself, every millisecond. Your phone can be off or away. You don't write any code.</p>
    {%- comment -%} Script anatomy diagram, inline SVG, stacked so it reads on phones. {%- endcomment -%}
    <figure class="m2-fig m2-fig--diagram">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 340 300" width="340" height="300" role="img" aria-labelledby="m2-sa-t m2-sa-d" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto">
        <title id="m2-sa-t">The parts of a Script</title>
        <desc id="m2-sa-d">A, When: you hold R2. B, Do this: tap R2 for 40 ms, wait 40 ms, repeat. C, the console sees fast, even taps.</desc>
        <defs><marker id="m2-ah2" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="5" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" fill="#62B8FF"/></marker></defs>
        <g font-family="inherit" font-size="15" fill="#E9EEF6">
          <rect x="20" y="10" width="300" height="70" rx="14" fill="#11192A" stroke="#298DDF" stroke-width="2"/>
          <circle cx="50" cy="45" r="15" fill="#298DDF"/><text x="50" y="50" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">A</text>
          <text x="78" y="40" font-weight="700">When</text><text x="78" y="62" fill="#9FB0C8" font-size="13">Over and over while I hold R2</text>
          <line x1="170" y1="82" x2="170" y2="104" stroke="#62B8FF" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#m2-ah2)"/>
          <rect x="20" y="112" width="300" height="70" rx="14" fill="#11192A" stroke="#298DDF" stroke-width="2"/>
          <circle cx="50" cy="147" r="15" fill="#298DDF"/><text x="50" y="152" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">B</text>
          <text x="78" y="142" font-weight="700">Do this</text><text x="78" y="164" fill="#9FB0C8" font-size="13">Tap R2 for 40 ms, then wait 40 ms</text>
          <line x1="170" y1="184" x2="170" y2="206" stroke="#62B8FF" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#m2-ah2)"/>
          <rect x="20" y="214" width="300" height="70" rx="14" fill="#11192A" stroke="#298DDF" stroke-width="2"/>
          <circle cx="50" cy="249" r="15" fill="#298DDF"/><text x="50" y="254" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">C</text>
          <text x="78" y="244" font-weight="700">The console sees</text><text x="78" y="266" fill="#9FB0C8" font-size="13">fast, even trigger taps</text>
        </g>
      </svg>
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-X.1 — A rapid fire Script, part by part</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-explained--where-scripts-live">
    <h2>Where Scripts live</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>For the whole config:</b> <b>Settings</b> › <b>Advanced</b> › <b>Advanced Script Maker</b>. They run in every situation.</li>
      <li><b>For one gun:</b> <b>Settings</b> › <b>AI Scripts</b> › pick the gun. They switch on only while the EXO sees that gun. <a href="#p-auto-per-gun-scripts">Give each gun its own Scripts</a></li>
    </ul>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'exo2-ann-recorder.webp' | asset_url }}" width="786" height="1704" loading="lazy" alt="The Advanced Script Maker, Scripts tab: New script, Anti-Recoil Lab, Paste ready-made script, Record script, and the config's Scripts list with on and off switches. A: Record script.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-X.2 — Advanced Script Maker, Scripts tab</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>Letter</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody><tr><td><span class="m2-letter">A</span></td><td><b>Record script</b></td><td>"Records your buttons and sticks to make your own script." <a href="#p-scripts-recorder">Record a Script</a></td></tr></tbody></table>
    <p>From the top, the screen also has <b>New script</b> (<a href="#p-scripts-editor">build one</a>), <b>Anti-Recoil Lab</b> (<a href="#p-scripts-anti-recoil-lab">recoil</a>) and <b>Paste ready-made script</b> (<a href="#p-scripts-library">library</a>). Each Script in the list has its own on/off switch.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-explained--four-ways">
    <h2>Four ways to get a Script</h2>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Way</th><th>Best for</th><th>Page</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Way"><b>Paste ready-made script</b></td><td data-label="Best for">The common ones: rapid fire, auto sprint, drop shot. 33 to pick from.</td><td data-label="Page"><a href="#p-scripts-library">Ready-made Scripts</a></td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Way"><b>Record script</b></td><td data-label="Best for">A combo you can already do with your hands.</td><td data-label="Page"><a href="#p-scripts-recorder">Record a Script</a></td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Way"><b>New script</b></td><td data-label="Best for">Exact control over every step and time.</td><td data-label="Page"><a href="#p-scripts-editor">Advanced Script Maker</a></td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Way"><b>Paste a code someone sent me</b></td><td data-label="Best for">A Script a friend shared.</td><td data-label="Page"><a href="#p-scripts-share">Share Scripts with a code</a></td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-explained--fair-play">
    <h2>Fair play</h2>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--note"><p class="m2-call-label">Note</p><p>Follow the rules of each game, event and platform you play on. Tournament Mode switches every script off in one tap.</p></aside>
    <p>Tournament Mode is in Global Settings. Your remaps and aim settings stay on. <a href="#p-reference-fair-play">Fair play and Tournament Mode</a></p>
  </section>

