<article class="m2-page" id="p-scripts-editor" data-group="Buttons &amp; Scripts" data-title="Advanced Script Maker" data-time="6 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Buttons &amp; Scripts</p>
    <h1>Advanced Script Maker</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Build your own Script step by step, with no code.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Mouse &amp; keyboard</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Controller</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Advanced</span><span class="m2-time">6 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-editor--the-editor">
    <h2>The editor</h2>
    <p>Open <b>Settings</b> › <b>Advanced</b> › <b>Advanced Script Maker</b>, tap <b>New script</b>, and press the button that should start it. The editor opens. A sentence at the top always says what your Script does in plain words.</p>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'exo2-ann-smart-actions-3.webp' | asset_url }}" width="786" height="1704" loading="lazy" alt="The script editor. A: Name it. B: the When card, what starts it and how it plays, showing L2, while held, On and No tag. C: the Do this card with four steps: LT 120 ms, RT 120 ms, X 80 ms, Y 80 ms. D: Tap or Hold for the selected step, Tap for 80 ms. E: Add a button press.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-ED.1 — Advanced Script Maker, New script</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>Letter</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">A</span></td><td><b>Name it</b></td><td>Give the Script a name and notes.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">B</span></td><td><b>WHEN</b> — what starts it, and how it plays</td><td>The start button, how it plays, <b>On</b>/<b>Off</b> and a tag. <a href="#p-scripts-when-it-runs">When a Script runs</a></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">C</span></td><td><b>DO THIS</b> — tap a step to change it</td><td>The steps, in order. The total time shows under them.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">D</span></td><td><b>Tap</b> / <b>Hold</b></td><td>How the selected step presses its button, and for how long.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">E</span></td><td><b>Add a button press</b></td><td>Adds a step: pad buttons, triggers or a stick push.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-editor--build-one">
    <h2>Build a Script</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Tap <b>New script</b>. Press (or tap) the button that should start it (2 in the first picture).</li>
      <li>Give it a name (1). In <b>WHEN</b>, tap the behaviour chip (2), like <b>while held</b>, and pick how it plays.</li>
      <li>Tap <b>Add a button press</b> (1 in the last picture). Pick a tab (<b>Pad</b>, <b>Sticks</b>, and on mouse configs <b>Mouse</b> and <b>Keys</b>), then a button.</li>
      <li>With the step selected (4), pick <b>Tap</b> or <b>Hold</b> and set its time with <b>−</b> / <b>+</b> (5).</li>
      <li>Add a pause or a held button from the <b>Then</b> card: <b>Wait next</b>, <b>Hold</b>, <b>Switch config</b>.</li>
      <li>Repeat until the sentence at the top reads right. Tap <b>Done</b> (4).</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-sc-start-btn.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Which button starts it. 1: the Controller tab. 2: L2, tapped in the list.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-ED.2 — Which button starts it?</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Tabs</b></td><td>Mouse, Keyboard or Controller.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>A button</b></td><td>Tap the button that should start your Script, or just press it.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-sc-steps.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="The Script editor. 1: Name it. 2: while held. 3: On. 4: the fourth step tile, Y for 80 ms. 5: the Tap for slider, 80 ms. The sentence at the top reads: when you press L2, pull LT for 120 ms, then pull RT for 120 ms, then tap X for 80 ms, and 1 more.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-ED.3 — The Script editor, top</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Name it</b></td><td>Give your Script a name.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>How it plays</b></td><td>While held, once, toggle and more.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>On / Off</b></td><td>For this Script.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">4</span></td><td><b>Step tiles</b></td><td>Each tile is one step. Tap one to change it.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">5</span></td><td><b>Time</b></td><td>How long the press lasts, in ms.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-sc-add.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="The lower half of the editor. 1: Add a button press. 2: Feels human, adds a little natural variation. 3: Copy. 4: Done.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-ED.4 — The Script editor, bottom</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Add a button press</b></td><td>Pick the next button for your Script.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Feels human</b></td><td>Adds a little natural variation to the timing.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>Copy</b></td><td>Copies this Script as a share code.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">4</span></td><td><b>Done</b></td><td>Keeps the Script.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-editor--check-it-worked">
    <h2>Check it worked</h2>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--check"><p class="m2-call-label">Check it worked</p>
      <p>You're set when all of these are true:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>App:</b> your Script is in the <b>Scripts</b> list with its switch on.</li>
        <li><b>Game:</b> pressing its start button plays the steps the top sentence describes.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Not seeing one? <a href="#p-help-scripts">A script won't fire or won't stop</a></p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-editor--related">
    <h2>Related</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="#p-scripts-steps">Every Script step</a></li>
      <li><a href="#p-scripts-timing">Script timing and human variation</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</article>


<article class="m2-page" id="p-scripts-when-it-runs" data-group="Buttons &amp; Scripts" data-title="When a Script runs" data-time="3 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Buttons &amp; Scripts</p>
    <h1>When a Script runs</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Every way a Script can start, and the timings behind them.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Advanced</span><span class="m2-time">3 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-when-it-runs--gestures">
    <h2>How it starts</h2>
    <p>In the editor, tap the behaviour chip in <b>WHEN</b>. The sheet <b>When should this happen?</b> opens.</p>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Choice</th><th>Plays</th><th>Good for</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Choice"><b>When I press it</b></td><td data-label="Plays">Once</td><td data-label="Good for">Combos, one-press moves</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Choice"><b>When I press it quickly</b></td><td data-label="Plays">Once</td><td data-label="Good for">A tap does the Script, a hold does the normal action</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Choice"><b>When I hold it down</b></td><td data-label="Plays">Once</td><td data-label="Good for">A second job on a long press</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Choice"><b>When I tap it twice</b></td><td data-label="Plays">Once</td><td data-label="Good for">A double-tap shortcut</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Choice"><b>When I let go of it</b></td><td data-label="Plays">Once</td><td data-label="Good for">Something after you release</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Choice"><b>Over and over while I hold it</b></td><td data-label="Plays">Repeats</td><td data-label="Good for">Rapid fire</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Choice"><b>Only while I hold it</b></td><td data-label="Plays">Holds</td><td data-label="Good for">Anti-recoil while firing</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Choice"><b>Until I press it again</b></td><td data-label="Plays">Stays on</td><td data-label="Good for">Toggles, like auto-run</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <p>A few choices only show if your EXO supports them.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-when-it-runs--timings">
    <h2>Press timings</h2>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>What it does</th><th>Range</th><th>Default</th><th>Start here</th><th>Raise it if…</th><th>Lower it if…</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Counts as held after</b></td><td data-label="What it does">How long a press must last to count as a hold.</td><td data-label="Range">100–2000 ms, step 50</td><td data-label="Default">350 ms</td><td data-label="Start here">350 ms</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Normal presses trigger the hold</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Holds feel slow to start</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Taps must land within</b></td><td data-label="What it does">The time allowed between the two taps of a double tap.</td><td data-label="Range">150–1000 ms, step 25</td><td data-label="Default">300 ms</td><td data-label="Start here">300 ms</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Your double taps get missed</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Two separate presses trigger it</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Counts as quick under</b></td><td data-label="What it does">How short a press must be to count as quick.</td><td data-label="Range">80–600 ms, step 10</td><td data-label="Default">250 ms</td><td data-label="Start here">250 ms</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Quick presses get missed</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Short holds count as quick</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-when-it-runs--conditions">
    <h2>On, Off, aiming and tags</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>On</b> / <b>Off</b>: switch the Script off without deleting it.</li>
      <li><b>When is this allowed to run?</b>: <b>Any time</b> (default), <b>Only hip-fire</b>, <b>Only aiming</b> or <b>Off</b>. Great for anti-recoil that should only run while you aim.</li>
      <li><b>No tag</b>: a label to keep Scripts organised (for example "Sniper"). It doesn't switch anything.</li>
    </ul>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--note"><p class="m2-call-label">Note</p><p>Tournament Mode stops every Script, whatever it's set to. Follow the rules of each game, event and platform you play on.</p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-when-it-runs--related">
    <h2>Related</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="#p-scripts-editor">Advanced Script Maker</a></li>
      <li><a href="#p-scripts-timing">Script timing and human variation</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</article>


<article class="m2-page" id="p-scripts-steps" data-group="Buttons &amp; Scripts" data-title="Every Script step" data-time="3 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Buttons &amp; Scripts</p>
    <h1>Every Script step</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Each kind of step you can add, with its ranges and defaults.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Advanced</span><span class="m2-time">3 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-steps--steps">
    <h2>Steps</h2>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>What it does</th><th>Fields</th><th>Range</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Step"><b>Button press</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Presses a button. <b>Tap</b> lets go after the time. <b>Hold</b> keeps it down.</td><td data-label="Fields"><b>Tap for</b></td><td data-label="Range">1–10000 ms (the slider goes to 2000)</td><td data-label="Default">80 ms</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Step"><b>Trigger pull</b> (LT / RT, L2 / R2)</td><td data-label="What it does">Pulls a trigger. <b>Pull</b> or <b>Keep pulled</b>.</td><td data-label="Fields"><b>Pull for</b></td><td data-label="Range">1–10000 ms</td><td data-label="Default">120 ms</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Step"><b>Wait</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Pauses before the next step.</td><td data-label="Fields"><b>Wait for</b></td><td data-label="Range">0–10000 ms</td><td data-label="Default">120 ms</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Step"><b>Stick push</b> (Sticks tab)</td><td data-label="What it does">Pushes a stick in a direction. Tap <b>Add this stick push</b>.</td><td data-label="Fields"><b>Left stick</b> / <b>Right stick</b>, <b>Direction</b>, <b>How far</b>, <b>How long</b></td><td data-label="Range">0–359°; 5–100 % (step 5); 20–2000 ms</td><td data-label="Default">Right stick, 90°, 50 %, 100 ms</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Step"><b>Hold</b> / <b>Let go</b> (Then card)</td><td data-label="What it does">Keeps a button down until a later <b>Let go</b>.</td><td data-label="Fields">—</td><td data-label="Range">No time setting</td><td data-label="Default">—</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Step"><b>Switch config</b> (Then card)</td><td data-label="What it does">Changes to another config. Shows when you have more than one.</td><td data-label="Fields"><b>Next</b> / <b>Before</b> / <b>Number</b></td><td data-label="Range">Config number</td><td data-label="Default">Next</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <p>There's no "repeat" step. To repeat, choose <b>Over and over while I hold it</b> in <a href="#p-scripts-when-it-runs">When a Script runs</a>, or set <b>How many times</b> in <a href="#p-scripts-timing">Timing and safety</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-steps--related">
    <h2>Related</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="#p-scripts-editor">Advanced Script Maker</a></li>
      <li><a href="#p-recipes-rapid-fire">Recipe: rapid fire</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</article>


<article class="m2-page" id="p-scripts-timing" data-group="Buttons &amp; Scripts" data-title="Script timing and human variation" data-time="3 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Buttons &amp; Scripts</p>
    <h1>Script timing</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Make Scripts exact, or human, and set when they give up or can fire again.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Advanced</span><span class="m2-time">3 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-timing--per-script">
    <h2>Timing and safety (one Script)</h2>
    <p>In the editor, tap the timing banner. It reads <b>Feels human</b> or <b>Exact timing</b>. The sheet <b>Timing and safety</b> opens.</p>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>What it does</th><th>Range</th><th>Default</th><th>Start here</th><th>Raise it if…</th><th>Lower it if…</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Human timing</b> / <b>Exact timing</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Human adds small, natural changes to each run. Exact plays every step to the millisecond.</td><td data-label="Range">Human / Exact</td><td data-label="Default">Human</td><td data-label="Start here">Human</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">—</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">—</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Wobble by up to</b></td><td data-label="What it does">How much each wait can change, run to run.</td><td data-label="Range">0–500 ms, step 5</td><td data-label="Default">15 ms</td><td data-label="Start here">15 ms</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Runs feel robotic</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">A combo needs exact timing</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Stick variance</b></td><td data-label="What it does">How much stick pushes change, run to run.</td><td data-label="Range">±0–10 %</td><td data-label="Default">±1 %</td><td data-label="Start here">±1 %</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">—</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Stick moves miss their mark</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Give up after</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Stops a running Script after this long.</td><td data-label="Range">100–30000 ms, step 500</td><td data-label="Default">10000 ms</td><td data-label="Start here">10000 ms</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">A long Script gets cut short</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">A stuck Script runs too long</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Never give up</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Lets a repeating Script run as long as you hold it.</td><td data-label="Range">On / Off</td><td data-label="Default">Off</td><td data-label="Start here">Off</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">—</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">—</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Wait before it can fire again</b></td><td data-label="What it does">A cool-down between runs.</td><td data-label="Range">0–60000 ms, step 50</td><td data-label="Default">200 ms</td><td data-label="Start here">200 ms</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">It fires twice by accident</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">It ignores fast repeat presses</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>How many times</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Plays a play-once Script this many times in a row.</td><td data-label="Range">1–10</td><td data-label="Default">1</td><td data-label="Start here">1</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">You want it repeated</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">—</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Always finish</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Plays to the end even if you let go early.</td><td data-label="Range">On / Off</td><td data-label="Default">Off</td><td data-label="Start here">Off</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Combos break when you let go</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">—</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-timing--per-config">
    <h2>Script timings (whole config)</h2>
    <p>Where: <b>Settings</b> › <b>Advanced</b> › <b>Translation</b> › <b>Script timings</b> ("Natural timing for your scripts, so no two runs are identical").</p>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>What it does</th><th>Range</th><th>Default</th><th>Start here</th><th>Raise it if…</th><th>Lower it if…</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Wait variation</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Changes every wait by up to this share.</td><td data-label="Range">0–50 %</td><td data-label="Default">0 %</td><td data-label="Start here">0 %</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">You want more natural timing</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Combos need exact timing</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Aim actions</b> (Advanced)</td><td data-label="What it does">"Magnitude: how much each push varies."</td><td data-label="Range">0.5–10 %, step 0.5</td><td data-label="Default">1 %</td><td data-label="Start here">1 %</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">—</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Aim Scripts feel uneven</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Aim angle</b> (Advanced)</td><td data-label="What it does">How much each push's direction varies.</td><td data-label="Range">0–15°, step 0.5</td><td data-label="Default">0°</td><td data-label="Start here">0°</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">—</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Pushes drift sideways</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Recoil strength wobble</b> (Advanced)</td><td data-label="What it does">How much anti-recoil strength varies.</td><td data-label="Range">0–100 %, step 5</td><td data-label="Default">0 %</td><td data-label="Start here">0 %</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">—</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Recoil control feels uneven</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-timing--related">
    <h2>Related</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="#p-scripts-when-it-runs">When a Script runs</a></li>
      <li><a href="#p-aim-smoothing-and-sync--sync-to-game">Sync to game</a> (same Translation screen)</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</article>


<article class="m2-page" id="p-scripts-recorder" data-group="Buttons &amp; Scripts" data-title="Record a Script" data-time="4 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Buttons &amp; Scripts</p>
    <h1>Record a Script</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Do a move once, and the EXO turns it into a Script you can replay with one button.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Mouse &amp; keyboard</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Controller</span><span class="m2-time">4 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-recorder--before-you-start">
    <h2>Before you start</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The EXO is connected to the app (the recorder checks first: "Checking your Core…").</li>
      <li>You can do the move on your controller, mouse or keyboard.</li>
      <li>The game is somewhere safe to practise, like a private match.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-recorder--choose-buttons">
    <h2>1. Choose start and stop buttons</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Open <b>Settings</b> › <b>Advanced</b> › <b>Advanced Script Maker</b>. Tap <b>Record script</b>.</li>
      <li>"Which button should <b>start</b> recording?" Press it on your device, or tap it under <b>Pad</b>, <b>Keyboard</b> or <b>Mouse</b>.</li>
      <li>"Which button should <b>stop</b> recording?" Tap <b>Same button</b>, or choose a different one.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'exo2-ann-recorder-2.webp' | asset_url }}" width="786" height="1704" loading="lazy" alt="Record a script: Which button should start recording? A: Pad, Keyboard and Mouse tabs. B: Press the button you want on your keyboard, mouse or controller, or tap it below; that press is not sent to the game. C: Cancel.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-REC.1 — Record a script, choose the start button</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>Letter</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">A</span></td><td><b>Pad</b> / <b>Keyboard</b> / <b>Mouse</b></td><td>Tap a button here instead of pressing it.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">B</span></td><td><b>Press the button you want</b></td><td>That press isn't recorded and the console won't see it.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">C</span></td><td><b>Cancel</b></td><td>Leave without recording.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-recorder--record">
    <h2>2. Record the move</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Press your start button. The app shows "Recording… press X to finish."</li>
      <li>Do the move once. Buttons, triggers and both sticks are recorded.</li>
      <li>Press your stop button. Recording also stops by itself after 60 seconds.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-sc-record.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Record a script: Which button should start recording. 1: press the button you want, it won't be recorded or sent to the console. 2: Cancel.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-REC.2 — Record script: pick the start button</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Start button</b></td><td>Press the button that starts recording. It isn't sent to the console.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Cancel</b></td><td>Stop without recording.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-recorder--save">
    <h2>3. Check it and pick the button that runs it</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Read "Here's what you did." Not right? Tap <b>Record again</b>.</li>
      <li>Tap <b>Next — choose the button that runs it</b>.</li>
      <li>Tap <b>Use</b> for the start button, or <b>Choose a different button</b>.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-sc-home.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="The Advanced Script Maker, Scripts tab. 1: New script. 2: Paste ready-made script. 3: Record script. 4: Scripts, the Scripts on this config.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-REC.3 — Advanced Script Maker: your new Script appears under Scripts (4)</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>New script</b></td><td>Build your own.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Paste ready-made script</b></td><td>Add one of the 33 ready-made Scripts.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>Record script</b></td><td>Play a move once and the EXO turns it into a Script.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">4</span></td><td><b>Scripts</b></td><td>Your Scripts on this config. Tap one to edit it.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <p>It's saved as "Recorded" plus the time. Open it in the Script list to rename it or tidy the steps.</p>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--note"><p class="m2-call-label">Note</p><p>Follow the rules of each game, event and platform you play on. Tournament Mode switches every script off in one tap.</p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-recorder--check-it-worked">
    <h2>Check it worked</h2>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--check"><p class="m2-call-label">Check it worked</p>
      <p>You're set when all of these are true:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>App:</b> a Script named "Recorded …" is in the Scripts list, switched on.</li>
        <li><b>Game:</b> pressing its button replays your move.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Not seeing one? <a href="#p-help-scripts">A script won't fire or won't stop</a></p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-recorder--next">
    <h2>Next</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Recommended:</b> <a href="#p-recipes-one-key-combo">Recipe: put a combo on one key</a></li>
      <li><a href="#p-scripts-editor">Advanced Script Maker</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</article>


<article class="m2-page" id="p-scripts-library" data-group="Buttons &amp; Scripts" data-title="Ready-made Scripts" data-time="4 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Buttons &amp; Scripts</p>
    <h1>Ready-made Scripts</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Add one of 33 ready-made Scripts in a few taps, then tune it.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Mouse &amp; keyboard</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Controller</span><span class="m2-time">4 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-library--add-one">
    <h2>1. Add a ready-made Script</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Open <b>Settings</b> › <b>Advanced</b> › <b>Advanced Script Maker</b>.</li>
      <li>Tap <b>Paste ready-made script</b> ("Pick one that is already built"), or the <b>Ready-made</b> tab.</li>
      <li>Pick a family chip (2), or start with <b>Featured</b>.</li>
      <li>Tap a Script, then choose which button starts it.</li>
      <li>Set its values, then tap <b>Add to this config</b> (3).</li>
    </ol>
    <p>You can change anything about it afterwards in the editor. Nothing fits? Tap <b>Nothing fits? Record your own</b>.</p>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-sc-ready.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="The Ready-made tab. Featured: Aim assist booster, Rapid fire already on R2, Turn assist. 1: Rapid fire card. 2: the All 33 chip, with Aim 8, Firing 6, Quality of life 8 and Movement and access 11.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCRI-LIBR.1 — Advanced Script Maker › Ready-made</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>A ready-made Script</b></td><td>Tap to add it. "already on R2" means you have it on that button.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Family chips</b></td><td>All, Aim, Firing, Quality of life, Movement &amp; access.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-sc-library.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="The ready-made library by family. Aim: Aim assist booster, Anti-recoil, Anti-recoil aiming only, Recoil pattern. 1: Show all 8 in Aim. Firing: Rapid fire (turbo), Burst fire.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCRI-LIBR.2 — The ready-made library, by family</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Show all</b></td><td>Every Script in this family.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-sc-setup.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="The Aim assist booster sheet. 1: Started by your Aim button, L2 pulled. 2: How strong, Medium. 3: Add to this config.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCRI-LIBR.3 — A ready-made Script's sheet</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Which button should start it?</b></td><td>Tap to change.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Its settings</b></td><td>A few values, like how strong it is.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>Add to this config</b></td><td>Adds it.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-library--the-list">
    <h2>All 33 ready-made Scripts</h2>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Scripts</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Category"><b>Movement &amp; access</b> (11)</td><td data-label="Scripts">Auto sprint · Auto walk forward · Crouch without holding it · Aim without holding it · Hold any button for me · Cook and throw a grenade · Easy melee · Slide cancel · Bunny hop · Reload and back off · Turn assist</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Category"><b>Aim</b> (8)</td><td data-label="Scripts">Aim assist booster · Anti-recoil · Anti-recoil, aiming only · Recoil pattern · Steady aim · Snap-to-target nudge · Quick 180° turn · Vehicles and parachutes</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Category"><b>Firing</b> (6)</td><td data-label="Scripts">Rapid fire (turbo) · Burst fire · Fire without holding · Hair trigger fire · Drop shot · Jump shot</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Category"><b>Quality of life</b> (8)</td><td data-label="Scripts">Swap and get back on target · Cancel a reload · Auto ping (Warzone only) · Ping your team · Menu skip · Looting · Two-button combo · Switch to my next config</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <p><b>Featured</b> holds the three most people want: Aim assist booster, Rapid fire and Turn assist. Your own stick always wins: aim Scripts blend into your stick, they don't fight it.</p>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--note"><p class="m2-call-label">Note</p><p>GPC scripts: coming soon.</p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-library--fair-play">
    <h2>Fair play</h2>
    <p>Follow the rules of each game, event and platform you play on. Tournament Mode switches every script off in one tap.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-library--check-it-worked">
    <h2>Check it worked</h2>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--check"><p class="m2-call-label">Check it worked</p>
      <p>You're set when all of these are true:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>App:</b> the Script shows in the <b>Scripts</b> list with its switch on.</li>
        <li><b>Game:</b> its button does the job, for example Auto sprint keeps you running after one click.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Not seeing one? <a href="#p-help-scripts">A script won't fire or won't stop</a></p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-library--next">
    <h2>Next</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Recommended:</b> <a href="#p-scripts-share">Share Scripts with a code</a></li>
      <li><a href="#p-recipes-rapid-fire">Recipes</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</article>


<article class="m2-page" id="p-scripts-share" data-group="Buttons &amp; Scripts" data-title="Share Scripts with a code" data-time="2 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Buttons &amp; Scripts</p>
    <h1>Share Scripts with a code</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Send a Script to a friend as a code, or paste one they sent you.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Mouse &amp; keyboard</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Controller</span><span class="m2-time">2 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-share--copy">
    <h2>1. Copy a Script's code</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Open the Script in the Advanced Script Maker.</li>
      <li>Scroll to the bottom and tap <b>Copy</b> (1).</li>
      <li>Paste the code into a message to your friend. Codes start with <b>ZSA2.</b></li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-sc-copy.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="A Script open in the editor, scrolled to the bottom. 1: the Copy button, next to Done.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-SH.1 — The Script editor, bottom</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Copy</b></td><td>Puts this Script on your clipboard as a code. Paste it into a message.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-share--paste">
    <h2>2. Paste a code someone sent you</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Copy the code on your phone.</li>
      <li>In the Advanced Script Maker (or a gun's page), tap <b>Paste a code someone sent me</b>.</li>
      <li>Read the toast, for example "Pasted onto R2, scaled from the maker's game settings to yours".</li>
      <li>Open the Script, check it over, then save it.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-sc-paste.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="The Advanced Script Maker, Scripts tab, scrolled down. 1: Paste a code someone sent me.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-SH.2 — Advanced Script Maker, bottom (newer build)</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Paste a code someone sent me</b></td><td>Copy the code from the message first, then tap here.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'exo2-ann-smart-actions-2.webp' | asset_url }}" width="786" height="1704" loading="lazy" alt="A gun's Scripts list. A: Rapid fire with its switch on. B: Paste a code someone sent me. C: New script, advanced.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-SH.3 — A gun's Scripts list</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>Letter</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">A</span></td><td>A Script's switch</td><td>Turns that Script on or off.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">B</span></td><td><b>Paste a code someone sent me</b></td><td>Adds a shared Script from a code.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">C</span></td><td><b>New script (advanced)</b></td><td>Opens the editor.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--note"><p class="m2-call-label">Note</p><p>Only Scripts have share codes. Configs don't. To pass a whole config on, use Copy and Paste on the Device page. <a href="#p-app-configs">Configs</a></p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-share--check-it-worked">
    <h2>Check it worked</h2>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--check"><p class="m2-call-label">Check it worked</p>
      <p>You're set when all of these are true:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>App:</b> the toast says "Pasted onto …" and the Script is in your list.</li>
        <li><b>Game:</b> the Script runs on the button the toast named.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>"That does not look like a ZeroStick button code"? Copy the whole code again. <a href="#p-help-scripts">Script problems</a></p></aside>
  </section>
</article>


<article class="m2-page" id="p-scripts-anti-recoil-lab" data-group="Buttons &amp; Scripts" data-title="Anti-Recoil Lab" data-time="8 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Buttons &amp; Scripts</p>
    <h1>Anti-Recoil Lab</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">You'll make a Script that pulls against your gun's recoil, so it stays on target.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Mouse &amp; keyboard</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Controller</span><span class="m2-time">8 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-anti-recoil-lab--before-you-start">
    <h2>Before you start</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your in-game settings match the app's list. <a href="#p-aim-game-settings">Set your in-game settings</a></li>
      <li>You can fire at a wall in the game (a firing range or private match).</li>
      <li>For one gun only, open the Lab from that gun's page in <b>AI Scripts</b>. <a href="#p-auto-per-gun-scripts">Per-gun Scripts</a></li>
    </ul>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--note"><p class="m2-call-label">Note</p><p>Follow the rules of each game, event and platform you play on. Tournament Mode switches every script off in one tap.</p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-anti-recoil-lab--pick-a-way">
    <h2>1. Pick a way to make it</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Open <b>Settings</b> › <b>Advanced</b> › <b>Advanced Script Maker</b>, or a gun's page.</li>
      <li>Tap <b>Anti-Recoil Lab</b> ("Trace a gun's recoil and cancel it out").</li>
      <li>Under <b>How do you want to make it?</b>, pick one of the three below.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'exo2-ann-recoil.webp' | asset_url }}" width="786" height="1704" loading="lazy" alt="Anti-Recoil Lab, How do you want to make it? A: Automatic, Recommended. B: Manual. C: Pull down. Below: Trace with your mouse's reticle instead, and Cancel.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-LAB.1 — Anti-Recoil Lab, first page</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>Letter</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">A</span></td><td><b>Automatic</b></td><td>"Your Core finds your gun's fire rate and builds your recoil curve for you." Warzone and MW4 only.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">B</span></td><td><b>Manual</b></td><td>"Set the fire rate, fire at a wall, then trace each shot mark in your game."</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">C</span></td><td><b>Pull down</b></td><td>"The regular anti-recoil: pulls straight down at the speed you set. No wall needed."</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-lab-bo2.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Anti-Recoil Lab in Black Ops II. Automatic isn't supported: this game's recoil is random. 1: Standard pull-down, For this game.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-LAB.2 — Anti-Recoil Lab in Black Ops II</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Standard pull-down</b></td><td>A steady pull while you hold Fire. Turn it up or down until the gun stays still.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Way</th><th>Works in</th><th>Best for</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Way"><b>Pull down</b></td><td data-label="Works in">Every game</td><td data-label="Best for">Controller players. No setup: tune it while you fire.</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Way"><b>Automatic</b></td><td data-label="Works in">Warzone and Modern Warfare 4 only. Greyed out in other games.</td><td data-label="Best for">An exact recoil curve with the least work.</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Way"><b>Manual</b></td><td data-label="Works in">Every game</td><td data-label="Best for">An exact curve in games without Automatic.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <p><b>Black Ops II</b> has random recoil, so it offers only <b>Standard pull-down</b>: "A steady pull down while you hold Fire."</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-anti-recoil-lab--pull-down">
    <h2>2a. Pull down (controller)</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Tap <b>Pull down</b>, then <b>Start</b>.</li>
      <li>In the game, hold Fire at any surface where you can see your shots.</li>
      <li>Shots still climb? Tap <b>+</b> on <b>Pull down</b>. Dipping? Tap <b>−</b>.</li>
      <li>Drifting sideways? Adjust <b>Pull sideways</b>: minus pulls left, plus pulls right.</li>
      <li>Fire again until the gun stays still. Tap <b>Accept</b>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>While this page is open, the D-pad tunes it: up / down changes Pull down, left / right changes Pull sideways. The D-pad does nothing in the game meanwhile.</p>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'exo2-ann-recoil-pull-down.webp' | asset_url }}" width="786" height="1640" loading="lazy" alt="Anti-Recoil Lab Pull down tune page. 1: Hold Fire to test it. 2: Pull down at 25 percent, more if your shots still climb. 3: Pull sideways at 0 percent, minus pulls left, plus pulls right. 4: Start delay at 0 ms. Below: Strength over the magazine, with Start and Middle at 100 percent.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-LAB.3 — Anti-Recoil Lab, Pull down live-tune (EXO connected)</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>Number</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">1</span></td><td><b>Hold Fire to test it</b></td><td>Fire at a wall. This line shows the EXO pulling while you shoot.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">2</span></td><td><b>Pull down</b></td><td>Tap + if your shots still climb, − if they now dip.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">3</span></td><td><b>Pull sideways</b></td><td>Minus pulls left, plus pulls right.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">4</span></td><td><b>Start delay</b></td><td>Waits this long after you start firing before pulling.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-lab-pad-tune.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Anti-Recoil Lab, controller live tune. 1: Hold Fire to test it. 2: Pull down 25 percent. 3: Pull sideways 0 percent. 4: Start delay 0 ms.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-LAB.4 — Pull down, live tune (controller)</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Hold Fire</b></td><td>Hold Fire at a plain wall. This line shows the pull.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Pull down</b></td><td>+ if your shots still climb, − if they dip.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>Pull sideways</b></td><td>Minus pulls left, plus pulls right.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">4</span></td><td><b>Start delay</b></td><td>Wait this long after you start firing.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-lab-pad-accept.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Lower half of the tune page. 1: Strength over the magazine, Middle 100 percent. 2: Only while aiming down sights switch, and the D-pad tip. 3: Accept.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-LAB.5 — Pull down, strength over the magazine</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Strength over the magazine</b></td><td>More or less pull at the start, middle and end.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Only while aiming down sights</b></td><td>Pull only while you aim. Your D-pad also nudges the pull.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>Accept</b></td><td>Saves it as a Script on your Fire button.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>What it does</th><th>Range</th><th>Default</th><th>Start here</th><th>Raise it if…</th><th>Lower it if…</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Pull down</b></td><td data-label="What it does">How hard it pulls down while you fire.</td><td data-label="Range">0–100 %</td><td data-label="Default">25 %</td><td data-label="Start here">25 %</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Shots still climb</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Shots dip below the target</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Pull sideways</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Minus pulls left, plus pulls right.</td><td data-label="Range">−100 to 100 %</td><td data-label="Default">0 %</td><td data-label="Start here">0 %</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Shots drift left</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Shots drift right</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Start delay</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Wait after you start firing before pulling.</td><td data-label="Range">0–2000 ms</td><td data-label="Default">0 ms</td><td data-label="Start here">0 ms</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">The first shots dip</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">The first shots climb</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Start</b> / <b>Middle</b> / <b>End</b> (Strength over the magazine)</td><td data-label="What it does">Pull strength for the first shots, half way, and the last shots.</td><td data-label="Range">0–200 % each</td><td data-label="Default">100 % each</td><td data-label="Start here">100 %</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">That part of the spray climbs</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">That part dips</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Spray lasts</b></td><td data-label="What it does">How long a full spray takes, for the Start-Middle-End shape.</td><td data-label="Range">0.5–10 s</td><td data-label="Default">3 s</td><td data-label="Start here">Your magazine's length</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">—</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">—</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Setting"><b>Only while aiming down sights</b></td><td data-label="What it does">Pulls only while you aim.</td><td data-label="Range">On / Off</td><td data-label="Default">Off</td><td data-label="Start here">Off</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Turn on if hip-fire gets pulled too</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">—</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <p><b>Accept</b> saves a Script named "Anti-recoil" that runs while Fire is held.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-anti-recoil-lab--automatic">
    <h2>2b. Automatic (Warzone and MW4)</h2>
    <p>The Lab walks you through 5 steps: <b>1 Check</b> · <b>2 Fire rate</b> · <b>3 Fire</b> · <b>4 Confirm</b> · <b>5 Tune</b>. Your HDMI must go through the EXO.</p>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li><b>Check:</b> confirm your game settings and switch on <b>I've checked my game settings</b>.</li>
      <li><b>Fire rate:</b> type the gun's fire rate (60–3000 RPM), or measure it by firing a full magazine.</li>
      <li><b>Fire:</b> tap <b>Start</b> and fire one magazine at the wall. "Your Core only watches."</li>
      <li><b>Confirm:</b> check the line the EXO traced. Drag a tick to fix a shot. Tap <b>Make the Script</b>.</li>
      <li><b>Tune:</b> adjust <b>Scale Y</b> and <b>Scale X</b> (0–400 %, default 100 %), then <b>Test it with the gun</b>. Tap <b>Done</b>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p><b>MW4:</b> do this in the Firing Range, where the EXO reads the ammo counter. Face a lit wall with a door, a sign or lane numbers on it. Keep the moving targets out of view.</p>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'exo2-ann-recoil-2.webp' | asset_url }}" width="786" height="1704" loading="lazy" alt="Anti-Recoil Lab step 4, Confirm. A: the step tabs 1 Check, 2 Fire rate, 3 Fire, 4 Confirm, 5 Tune. B: Traced your magazine, 26 shots along the line; drag a tick to move it, or tap it for the arrows. C: the traced shot pattern drawn over the game picture.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-LAB.6 — Anti-Recoil Lab, Automatic, step 4 Confirm</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-lab-auto-fire.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Automatic, step 3 Fire: in the Firing Range, face the wall, aim down sights, press Start and hold Fire until the magazine is empty. 1: Start.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-LAB.7 — Automatic, 3 Fire</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Start</b></td><td>Then hold Fire until the magazine is empty. Keep still.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-lab-auto-found.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Automatic, step 4 Confirm: Mapped your magazine, 26 bullets, each one numbered on the wall where it hit. Drag a dot to move it.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-LAB.8 — Automatic, 4 Confirm</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>Letter</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">A</span></td><td>Step tabs</td><td>Where you are in the 5 steps.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">B</span></td><td><b>Traced your magazine</b></td><td>How many shots the EXO found along the line.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter">C</span></td><td>The trace</td><td>Each numbered tick is one shot. Drag one to move it.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--important"><p class="m2-call-label">Important</p><p>Automatic for MW4 is new. Always run <b>Test it with the gun</b> before you rely on it. If the trace looks wrong, tap <b>Use Manual instead</b>.</p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-anti-recoil-lab--manual">
    <h2>2c. Manual (any game)</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Tap <b>Manual</b>. Steps: <b>Check</b> · <b>Fire rate</b> · <b>Fire pattern</b> · <b>Model</b>.</li>
      <li>Set the fire rate, then fire a magazine at a wall.</li>
      <li>Trace each shot mark you see in the game.</li>
      <li>On <b>Your recoil model</b>, adjust <b>Scale X</b>, <b>Scale Y</b> and <b>Optimization level</b> (0–10).</li>
      <li>Tap <b>Accept</b>. Manual saves only when you press Accept.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-lab-man-check.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Manual, step 1 Check: other bindings that fire are paused, Pass-through is off, Mouse DPI 1000, your in-game settings match, a private match or training area. 1: I've checked my game settings. 2: Start.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-LAB.9 — Manual, 1 Check</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>I've checked my game settings</b></td><td>Switch on once your game matches this config.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Start</b></td><td>Goes to the next step.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-lab-man-pattern.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Manual, step 3 Fire pattern: Fire pattern modification Off, Small, Medium or Large, and the steps: fire a pattern at a wall aimed down sights, put your reticle on the first shot mark, press Trace, press your fire button on each next mark, press Done.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-LAB.10 — Manual, 3 Fire pattern</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-lab-man-trace.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Fire pattern modeling: 20 shots traced, a red dotted line climbing up. 1: Done. Also Reset and Keep it, fire another pattern.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-LAB.11 — Manual, tracing your shots</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Done</b></td><td>Tap when every shot is traced.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-lab-man-model.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Manual, step 4 Model: your recoil model against your traced shots, Fire to preview, Scale X 100 percent and Scale Y 100 percent.">
      <figcaption>Figure SCR-LAB.12 — Manual, 4 Model</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p>On a mouse config, the first page also offers <b>Trace with your mouse's reticle instead</b>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-anti-recoil-lab--check-it-worked">
    <h2>Check it worked</h2>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--check"><p class="m2-call-label">Check it worked</p>
      <p>You're set when all of these are true:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>App:</b> a recoil Script (like "Anti-recoil") is in the Scripts list, switched on.</li>
        <li><b>Game:</b> hold Fire at a wall for a full magazine: the shots stay in a tight group.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Not seeing one? <a href="#p-help-scripts">A script won't fire or won't stop</a></p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-scripts-anti-recoil-lab--related">
    <h2>Related</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="#p-recipes-simple-anti-recoil">Recipe: simple anti-recoil</a></li>
      <li><a href="#p-auto-per-gun-scripts">Give each gun its own Scripts</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</article>


<article class="m2-page" id="p-recipes-rapid-fire" data-group="Buttons &amp; Scripts" data-title="Recipe: rapid fire" data-time="3 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Buttons &amp; Scripts · Recipe</p>
    <h1>Rapid fire for semi-auto guns</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Hold Fire and the EXO taps it for you, over and over.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Mouse &amp; keyboard</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Controller</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">PS5 · Xbox · PC</span><span class="m2-time">3 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-recipes-rapid-fire--what-you-need">
    <h2>What you need</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A config for your game. Fire on R2 / RT (or your mouse's left click mapped to it).</li>
      <li>Follow the rules of each game, event and platform you play on. Tournament Mode switches every script off in one tap.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-recipes-rapid-fire--add-it">
    <h2>Add it</h2>
    <p><b>Option A, ready-made (fastest):</b></p>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>In the Advanced Script Maker, tap <b>Paste ready-made script</b>.</li>
      <li>Under <b>Firing</b>, tap <b>Rapid fire (turbo)</b>.</li>
      <li>Keep Fire as the start button. Tap <b>Add to this config</b>.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-sc-library.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="The ready-made library: Aim family, Show all 8 in Aim, then the Firing family with Rapid fire (turbo) and Burst fire.">
      <figcaption>Figure RAPI-FIRE.1 — Ready-made library: Rapid fire (turbo) under Firing</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Show all</b></td><td>Every Script in that family.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <p><b>Option B, build it:</b> <b>New script</b> on Fire, set <b>Over and over while I hold it</b>, then add a Fire <b>Tap</b> for 40 ms and a <b>Wait</b> of 40 ms. <a href="#p-scripts-editor">Advanced Script Maker</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-recipes-rapid-fire--values-to-tune">
    <h2>Values to tune</h2>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Value</th><th>Range</th><th>Start here</th><th>Shorter</th><th>Longer</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Value"><b>Time between taps</b></td><td data-label="Range">15–300 ms, step 5</td><td data-label="Start here">40 ms</td><td data-label="Shorter">Faster shots. Too fast and games drop shots.</td><td data-label="Longer">Slower, steadier shots</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-recipes-rapid-fire--check-it-worked">
    <h2>Check it worked</h2>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--check"><p class="m2-call-label">Check it worked</p>
      <p>You're set when all of these are true:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>App:</b> Rapid fire is in the Scripts list, switched on.</li>
        <li><b>Game:</b> in a firing range, hold Fire with a semi-auto gun for 3 seconds: it keeps firing.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Not seeing one? <a href="#p-help-scripts">A script won't fire or won't stop</a></p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-recipes-rapid-fire--variations">
    <h2>Variations</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Only on one gun: add it from that gun's page in AI Scripts. <a href="#p-auto-per-gun-scripts">Per-gun Scripts</a></li>
      <li>A fixed number of shots per press: use <b>Burst fire</b> instead.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</article>


<article class="m2-page" id="p-recipes-simple-anti-recoil" data-group="Buttons &amp; Scripts" data-title="Recipe: simple anti-recoil" data-time="3 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Buttons &amp; Scripts · Recipe</p>
    <h1>Simple anti-recoil</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">A steady pull down while you fire, tuned live with no setup.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Controller</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">PS5 · Xbox · PC</span><span class="m2-time">3 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-recipes-simple-anti-recoil--what-you-need">
    <h2>What you need</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A config for your game and a wall to shoot at.</li>
      <li>Follow the rules of each game, event and platform you play on. Tournament Mode switches every script off in one tap.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-recipes-simple-anti-recoil--add-it">
    <h2>Add it</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Open <b>Anti-Recoil Lab</b> (Advanced Script Maker, or a gun's page).</li>
      <li>Tap <b>Pull down</b>, then <b>Start</b>.</li>
      <li>Hold Fire at a wall. Tap <b>+</b> on <b>Pull down</b> until the shots stop climbing.</li>
      <li>Tap <b>Accept</b>.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-lab-pad-start.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Anti-Recoil Lab on a controller config: make anti-recoil for a gun, find a plain wall 10 to 15 m away, press Start, then hold Fire. 1: Only while aiming down sights switch. 2: Start.">
      <figcaption>Figure ANTI-RECO.1 — Anti-Recoil Lab, controller</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Only while aiming down sights</b></td><td>Pull only while you aim.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Start</b></td><td>Then hold Fire at the wall.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <p>Full details: <a href="#p-scripts-anti-recoil-lab--pull-down">Pull down in the Anti-Recoil Lab</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-recipes-simple-anti-recoil--values-to-tune">
    <h2>Values to tune</h2>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Value</th><th>Range</th><th>Start here</th><th>Raise it if…</th><th>Lower it if…</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Value"><b>Pull down</b></td><td data-label="Range">0–100 %</td><td data-label="Start here">25 %</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Shots still climb</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Shots dip</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Value"><b>Pull sideways</b></td><td data-label="Range">−100 to 100 %</td><td data-label="Start here">0 %</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">Shots drift left</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">Shots drift right</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-recipes-simple-anti-recoil--check-it-worked">
    <h2>Check it worked</h2>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--check"><p class="m2-call-label">Check it worked</p>
      <p>You're set when all of these are true:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>App:</b> "Anti-recoil" is in the Scripts list, switched on.</li>
        <li><b>Game:</b> a full magazine at a wall lands in a tight group, not a line climbing up.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Not seeing one? <a href="#p-help-scripts">A script won't fire or won't stop</a></p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-recipes-simple-anti-recoil--variations">
    <h2>Variations</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Only while aiming: switch on <b>Only while aiming down sights</b>.</li>
      <li>Per gun: open the Lab from each gun's page. <a href="#p-auto-per-gun-scripts">Per-gun Scripts</a></li>
      <li>Exact pattern in Warzone or MW4: use <b>Automatic</b>. <a href="#p-scripts-anti-recoil-lab--automatic">Automatic</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</article>


<article class="m2-page" id="p-recipes-toggle-aim" data-group="Buttons &amp; Scripts" data-title="Recipe: tap to aim" data-time="2 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Buttons &amp; Scripts · Recipe</p>
    <h1>Tap to aim (instead of hold)</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Press aim once to stay aimed, with nothing held down.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Mouse &amp; keyboard</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Controller</span><span class="m2-time">2 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-recipes-toggle-aim--what-you-need">
    <h2>What you need</h2>
    <p>A config for your game. Many game packs already include <b>Aim hold</b> (the ready-made Aim without holding it), switched off. Look for it in the Scripts list first.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-recipes-toggle-aim--add-it">
    <h2>Add it</h2>
    <p><b>Option A, a true toggle:</b></p>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Open <b>Mappings</b> and tap your aim button's row (for example <b>L2</b>, or <b>Right click</b>).</li>
      <li>Tap <b>Behaves</b> and choose <b>On, then off</b>.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-mp-sends.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="A button's panel. 1: Sends. 2: Behaves, While I hold it. 3: the new output. 4: Unbind.">
      <figcaption>Figure TOGG-AIM.1 — A button's panel: Behaves is 2</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Sends</b></td><td>What the button does.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Behaves</b></td><td>Pick the toggle behaviour here.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>Output</b></td><td>Leave it as your aim button.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">4</span></td><td><b>Unbind</b></td><td>Sends nothing.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <p><b>Option B, ready-made:</b> add <b>Aim without holding it</b> from <b>Movement &amp; access</b>. One pull keeps you aimed for a set time.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-recipes-toggle-aim--values-to-tune">
    <h2>Values to tune</h2>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Value</th><th>Range</th><th>Start here</th><th>Raise it if…</th><th>Lower it if…</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Value"><b>Stay aimed for</b> (Option B)</td><td data-label="Range">1000–29000 ms, step 500</td><td data-label="Start here">6000 ms</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">You drop out of aim too soon</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">You stay aimed too long</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-recipes-toggle-aim--check-it-worked">
    <h2>Check it worked</h2>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--check"><p class="m2-call-label">Check it worked</p>
      <p>You're set when all of these are true:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>App:</b> the aim row shows <b>On, then off</b> (or the Script is switched on).</li>
        <li><b>Game:</b> tap aim once and let go: you stay aimed down sights.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Not seeing one? <a href="#p-help-scripts">A script won't fire or won't stop</a></p></aside>
  </section>
</article>


<article class="m2-page" id="p-recipes-auto-sprint" data-group="Buttons &amp; Scripts" data-title="Recipe: always sprint" data-time="2 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Buttons &amp; Scripts · Recipe</p>
    <h1>Always sprint</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Click sprint once and keep running without holding the stick forward.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Controller</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Mouse &amp; keyboard</span><span class="m2-time">2 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-recipes-auto-sprint--what-you-need">
    <h2>What you need</h2>
    <p>A config for your game, with sprint on L3 (or your sprint key).</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-recipes-auto-sprint--add-it">
    <h2>Add it</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>In the Advanced Script Maker, tap <b>Paste ready-made script</b>.</li>
      <li>Under <b>Movement &amp; access</b>, tap <b>Auto sprint</b>.</li>
      <li>Keep L3 as the start button, or pick your sprint button. Tap <b>Add to this config</b>.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-sc-ready.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="The Ready-made tab. 1: a Featured card. 2: the family chips, including Movement and access 11.">
      <figcaption>Figure AUTO-SPRI.1 — Ready-made: the Movement &amp; access chip is in row 2</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>A ready-made Script</b></td><td>Tap to add it.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Family chips</b></td><td>Tap Movement &amp; access.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <p>Your own sprint press still goes through. The Script only supplies the forward stick.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-recipes-auto-sprint--values-to-tune">
    <h2>Values to tune</h2>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Value</th><th>Range</th><th>Start here</th><th>Raise it if…</th><th>Lower it if…</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Value"><b>Keep running for</b></td><td data-label="Range">1000–29000 ms, step 500</td><td data-label="Start here">8000 ms</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">You stop before you get there</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">You run past where you meant to stop</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <p>It stops on its own at the end. Move the stick any time to take over.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-recipes-auto-sprint--check-it-worked">
    <h2>Check it worked</h2>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--check"><p class="m2-call-label">Check it worked</p>
      <p>You're set when all of these are true:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>App:</b> Auto sprint is in the Scripts list, switched on.</li>
        <li><b>Game:</b> click sprint once and let go of the stick: you keep running forward.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Not seeing one? <a href="#p-help-scripts">A script won't fire or won't stop</a></p></aside>
  </section>
</article>


<article class="m2-page" id="p-recipes-drop-shot" data-group="Buttons &amp; Scripts" data-title="Recipe: drop shot" data-time="2 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Buttons &amp; Scripts · Recipe</p>
    <h1>Drop shot</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Go to ground the moment you open fire. Your trigger keeps working.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Controller</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Mouse &amp; keyboard</span><span class="m2-time">2 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-recipes-drop-shot--what-you-need">
    <h2>What you need</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A config for your game. Know which button makes you crouch or go prone.</li>
      <li>Follow the rules of each game, event and platform you play on. Tournament Mode switches every script off in one tap.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-recipes-drop-shot--add-it">
    <h2>Add it</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>In the Advanced Script Maker, tap <b>Paste ready-made script</b>.</li>
      <li>Under <b>Firing</b>, tap <b>Drop shot</b>.</li>
      <li>Set <b>Crouch / prone button</b> to your game's button. Tap <b>Add to this config</b>.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-sc-setup.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="A ready-made Script's sheet. 1: the start button. 2: its settings. 3: Add to this config.">
      <figcaption>Figure DROP-SHOT.1 — A ready-made Script's sheet</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Start button</b></td><td>Tap to change.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Settings</b></td><td>Set your crouch or prone button here on Drop shot.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>Add to this config</b></td><td>Adds it.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-recipes-drop-shot--values-to-tune">
    <h2>Values to tune</h2>
    <div class="m2-table"><table class="m2-settings"><thead><tr><th>Value</th><th>Range</th><th>Start here</th><th>Raise it if…</th><th>Lower it if…</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Value"><b>How soon after you fire</b></td><td data-label="Range">0–800 ms, step 10</td><td data-label="Start here">40 ms</td><td data-label="Raise it if…">You drop before your first shot</td><td data-label="Lower it if…">You drop too late</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <p>Prefer to jump? <b>Jump shot</b> works the same way.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-recipes-drop-shot--check-it-worked">
    <h2>Check it worked</h2>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--check"><p class="m2-call-label">Check it worked</p>
      <p>You're set when all of these are true:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>App:</b> Drop shot is in the Scripts list, switched on.</li>
        <li><b>Game:</b> press Fire while standing: you go down and keep firing.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Not seeing one? <a href="#p-help-scripts">A script won't fire or won't stop</a></p></aside>
  </section>
</article>


<article class="m2-page" id="p-recipes-one-key-combo" data-group="Buttons &amp; Scripts" data-title="Recipe: a combo on one key" data-time="4 min">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Buttons &amp; Scripts · Recipe</p>
    <h1>Put a combo on one key</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Record a move once, then play it back with one button.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Mouse &amp; keyboard</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Controller</span><span class="m2-time">4 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-recipes-one-key-combo--what-you-need">
    <h2>What you need</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A spare button or key to run the combo.</li>
      <li>Follow the rules of each game, event and platform you play on. Tournament Mode switches every script off in one tap.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-recipes-one-key-combo--add-it">
    <h2>Add it</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Tap <b>Record script</b> in the Advanced Script Maker.</li>
      <li>Choose a start button and a stop button that the combo doesn't use.</li>
      <li>Press start, do the combo once, press stop.</li>
      <li>Check "Here's what you did.", then tap <b>Next — choose the button that runs it</b>.</li>
      <li>Pick your spare button.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-sc-record.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Record a script. 1: press the button that starts recording. 2: Cancel.">
      <figcaption>Figure KEY-COMB.1 — Record script</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Start button</b></td><td>Not sent to the console.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Cancel</b></td><td>Stop without recording.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <p>Full walkthrough: <a href="#p-scripts-recorder">Record a Script</a>. For just two buttons at once, the ready-made <b>Two-button combo</b> is quicker.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-recipes-one-key-combo--values-to-tune">
    <h2>Values to tune</h2>
    <p>Open the recorded Script in the editor. Tap any step to change its time, or use <b>Exact timing</b> in <a href="#p-scripts-timing">Timing and safety</a> for a precise combo.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-recipes-one-key-combo--check-it-worked">
    <h2>Check it worked</h2>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--check"><p class="m2-call-label">Check it worked</p>
      <p>You're set when all of these are true:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>App:</b> a "Recorded …" Script is in the list, on your spare button.</li>
        <li><b>Game:</b> one press plays the whole combo.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Not seeing one? <a href="#p-help-scripts">A script won't fire or won't stop</a></p></aside>
  </section>
</article>
